      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually - this makes sense.\n\nI think we need a follow on patch to detail some of this behavior. For example - consider the following case: \n\nUser A creates an *impersonated* trust with User B as the trustee, with role 1 on project 1. User A also has roles 1 and 2 and project 1, but they are only giving User B role 1. Even though impersonation is set to True, User B will only get role 1 on project 1 despite the fact they are suppose to impersonate User A.\n\nNot saying this need to be addressed in this patch - just marking it for discussion. Do we want to allow impersonation to be true impersonation between User A and User B where User B will actually get all roles that User A has on a project, i.e. making it so that impersonated trusts don\u0027t have roles specified? \n\nMidcycle topic?",
